---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import { helloEmail } from "../../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="HydroVault Terms of Service — scubadeving"
  description="Terms of service for HydroVault, a scuba cylinder management app by scubadeving."
  ogImage="/og-hydrovault.png"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24">

    <Header showBack={true} />

    <main>
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
          HydroVault Terms of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated: August 2026</p>
        <p class="mt-3 rounded-xl border border-amber-400/20 bg-amber-400/5 px-4 py-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-amber-400">
          This document is a working draft. It has not been reviewed by legal counsel.
          Do not rely on it as a final legal instrument — have it reviewed by a qualified
          attorney before public release.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="mb-24 space-y-12">

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            1. Agreement to terms
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            By downloading, installing, or using HydroVault ("the App"), you agree to be
            bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms,
            do not use the App.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            2. Description of service
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            HydroVault is a scuba cylinder maintenance tracking app that helps divers log
            hydrostatic test dates, visual inspection records, O₂ service history, and
            related cylinder maintenance events. Inspection interval guidance is derived
            from DOT (US) and EN 1975/EN 1964 (EU) regulatory standards. The App operates
            entirely offline and stores all data locally on your device.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            3. Equipment safety disclaimer
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">
              Read this section carefully.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              HydroVault is a <strong class="font-medium text-ink">record-keeping tool only</strong>.
              It does not perform physical inspections, certify equipment, or replace the
              judgment of a qualified cylinder inspector or dive professional.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              You are solely responsible for:
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 space-y-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted list-disc">
              <li>Ensuring all cylinders are inspected and tested by qualified professionals at intervals required by applicable law and manufacturer guidelines.</li>
              <li>Verifying that inspection intervals displayed by the App are accurate and applicable to your specific cylinders, jurisdiction, and use case.</li>
              <li>Never using a cylinder solely on the basis of App records — physical inspection by a qualified technician is always required.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              Inspection interval guidance in the App is informational and based on publicly
              available regulatory standards. It may not reflect jurisdiction-specific rules,
              manufacturer requirements, or recent regulatory changes. Always consult a
              qualified cylinder inspector or the relevant regulatory authority for binding
              guidance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            4. Permitted use
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            You may use the App for personal cylinder record-keeping. You may not: reverse
            engineer, decompile, or disassemble the App; redistribute or resell the App or
            its content; use the App in any way that violates applicable law; or present
            App records as official certification or inspection documentation.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            5. Intellectual property
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The App, including its design, code, and content, is the property of scubadeving
            and is protected by applicable intellectual property law. These Terms do not
            grant you any ownership rights in the App. Open-source components used in the
            App are governed by their respective licenses, which are disclosed within the App.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            6. Disclaimer of warranties
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The App is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind,
            express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability,
            fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy of inspection interval data, or
            non-infringement. scubadeving does not warrant that the App will be error-free,
            uninterrupted, or that its regulatory data is current or complete.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            7. Limitation of liability
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            To the fullest extent permitted by law, scubadeving shall not be liable for any
            indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from
            your use of or inability to use the App — including but not limited to personal
            injury, death, equipment failure, loss of data, or regulatory non-compliance —
            regardless of the theory of liability and even if scubadeving has been advised
            of the possibility of such damages.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            scubadeving's total liability to you for any claim arising from these Terms or
            your use of the App shall not exceed the amount you paid for the App in the
            twelve months preceding the claim.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            8. Governing law
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, United States,
            without regard to conflict of law principles. Any disputes arising under these
            Terms shall be resolved in the state or federal courts located in California.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            9. Changes to these terms
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            scubadeving reserves the right to update these Terms at any time. Updated Terms
            will be posted at this URL with a revised date. Continued use of the App after
            changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-muted">
            10. Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Questions about these Terms may be directed to{" "}
            <a
              href={`mailto:${helloEmail}`}
              class="rounded underline text-accent transition-colors focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"
            >
              {helloEmail}
            </a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />

  </div>
</Layout>
